Acceptance Criteria
AC1: Response Model Enhancement - Reuse Existing Structure
Given the API response model needs to include resource links
When GET /apis/{apiId} is called
Then response should include:

All existing API fields (unchanged)
New 
apiResourceLinks array with same structure as POST/PATCH
 

Each link includes: linkId, categoryId, subcategoryId, title, url
AC2: Service Layer Integration - Reuse Existing Logic
Given existing service methods for resource link retrieval
When processing GET request
Then reuse existing components:

Database query logic for fetching resource links
ApiResourceLink model structure
Category/subcategory mapping if needed
AC3: Database Query Enhancement - Efficient Retrieval
Given API ID is provided
When fetching API details
Then retrieve resource links in single query or optimized approach:

JOIN api_resource_links table with main API query
Order links by categoryId, subcategoryId for consistent response
Handle APIs with no resource links (empty array)
AC4: Response Format Consistency - Standard Structure
Given successful API retrieval
When returning response
Then maintain existing response format:

Same HTTP status codes
Same error handling patterns
Add apiResourceLinks as new field in existing response structure
AC5: Error Handling - Reuse Existing Patterns
Given API retrieval errors occur
When processing GET request
Then use existing error handling:

API not found: existing RecordNotFoundException handling
Database errors: existing exception handling patterns
No changes to existing error response format
AC6: Logging Standards - Enhanced for Resource Links
